@node Install
@chapter Install

@cindex Install

If manually installed then ensure that @code{mdired.el} is in @code{load-path}.

If installed via @code{package-install}@comma{} then all @strong{mdired} commands are auto-loaded.

@node Usage
@chapter Usage

@cindex Usage

@strong{mdired} provides different SIMD-style commands to operate on marked Dired items (@ref{Marks vs Flags,,,emacs,}).

Please be advised: @strong{mdired} can make irreversible changes to the file system if no prior checkpoint (typically via a source code management or backup tool) is available. Exercise caution.


@deffn Command mdired-do-command COMMAND
Run Elisp COMMAND on marked Dired items.

For all marked Dired items@comma{} call @code{find-file} and then run COMMAND on each item in sequential fashion. After this command has been run@comma{} any buffers that are modified will remain open and unsaved.

COMMAND may be an interactive command or a named keyboard macro.

Note: @code{mdired-do-command} does @emph{not} check if a marked Dired item is a file or directory. The marked Dired item should handle COMMAND gracefully.

If a COMMAND on a marked item results in an error@comma{} the error is ignored; COMMAND will still be run on all remaining marked items.
@end deffn

@deffn Command mdired-copy ARG
Copy current Dired item to marked Dired items with overwrite policy ARG@.

For all marked Dired items@comma{} copy the current Dired item to it. If the marked item is a directory@comma{} the current item is copied into it. If the marked item is a file@comma{} the current Dired item will write over it per the policy determined via the command prefix ARG@.

If no command prefix (@kbd{C-u}) is set@comma{} then the user will be prompted to select an overwrite policy as described in @code{copy-file}. The options provided are:

@itemize
@item
never : do not overwrite marked file
@item
overwrite : overwrite marked file
@item
ask : prompt user if marked file should be overwritten.
@end itemize

If the command prefix (@kbd{C-u}) is set@comma{} then marked files will be overwritten without prompt.
@end deffn

@deffn Command mdired-compile
Run @code{compile} on marked Dired directories.

For all marked directories@comma{} run @code{compile} on each directory@comma{} with output placed in a uniquely named buffer of the form

``@strong{compilation - %s}''

where ``%s'' is the name of the marked directory.

@code{mdired-compile} pre-checks that all marked items are directories and will not execute if not true.

Refer to @ref{Compilation,,,emacs,} for detail on @code{compile}.
@end deffn

@deffn Command mdired-byte-recompile
Byte recompile marked Elisp files or directories.

For all marked items@comma{} run either @code{byte-recompile-directory} if the item is a directory@comma{} or @code{byte-recompile-file} if the item is an Elisp file.
@end deffn

